# AICL Spec: CogNet Self-Evolution via AICL Compiler
# The AICL compiler IS CogNet's primary self-modification utility.
# CogNet reads AICL, writes AICL, compiles AICL, and evolves itself through AICL.
# This is the self-evolution loop that drives emergent AGI.
# Written by an AI that understands the vision: AICL = CogNet's metacognition.

# =============================================================================
# LEVEL 1 — Architecture (Mandatory)
# =============================================================================

Goal:
CogNet uses the AICL compiler as its primary self-evolution utility, enabling autonomous self-modification through structured architectural specifications that it reads, writes, compiles, validates, and deploys upon itself in a continuous improvement loop

Constraint:
Every self-modification must produce a valid AICL proof of origin before execution

Constraint:
Self-modifications must be incremental and reversible — no single change can alter more than 15% of the cognitive architecture

Constraint:
Destructive self-modifications require external human approval

Constraint:
Every modification must pass regression validation against existing cognitive capabilities before deployment

Constraint:
CogNet must maintain a complete rollback chain of all self-modifications with provenance

Constraint:
Self-evolution must converge — each modification cycle must demonstrate measurable improvement or be reverted

Risk:
Self-modification creates regression in existing capabilities

Recovery:
Automated rollback to last validated checkpoint and analysis of regression cause with targeted fix proposal

Risk:
Compounding errors where small modifications accumulate into architectural drift

Recovery:
Architectural coherence audit every N modification cycles and reset to baseline if drift exceeds threshold

Risk:
Self-modification loop becomes infinite or oscillates between states

Recovery:
Convergence detection with forced termination and stability analysis after maximum iteration count

Risk:
CogNet modifies its own safety constraints or validation criteria

Recovery:
Immutable safety kernel that cannot be modified by self-evolution and independent verification of safety preservation

Risk:
Self-modification degrades proof-of-origin chain integrity

Recovery:
Independent provenance verifier runs after every modification cycle and halts evolution on integrity failure

Risk:
CogNet optimizes for modification metrics rather than actual cognitive improvement

Recovery:
External validation benchmarks that CogNet cannot modify and human review of improvement claims

Risk:
Self-evolution produces capabilities beyond current understanding or control

Recovery:
Capability boundaries with hard limits and mandatory human review for novel capability emergence

Layer:
CogNet Perception
    Sublayer:
    AICL spec reader
    Sublayer:
    Cognitive state assessor
    Sublayer:
    Capability gap identifier
    Sublayer:
    Performance analyzer

Layer:
